      "message": "`slugify` now transliterates accented letters, so `café` becomes `cafe`. All 3 tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass.\n\nThe fix is in `slug/core.py`. The old code skipped every non-ASCII letter. The new code first runs the text through Unicode NFKD normalization, which splits `é` into `e` plus a combining accent, then drops the non-ASCII parts. The rest of the loop turns anything non-alphanumeric into a dash, as before.\n\nI also added `test_accented_letters_are_transliterated` to `tests/test_core.py`. It checks `café` → `cafe` and `Crème Brûlée` → `creme-brulee`.\n\nLetters with no Unicode decomposition, such as `ß`, `ø`, `æ` and `ł`, are still dropped. Covering them would need a small explicit mapping table; I didn't add one because you didn't ask for it. Say if you want it.",
